From 253f051bc325bfc283fbcb1ef4e89cc70e94de68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sami <247917809+0c33@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 04:33:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(gfx906): run the DFlash2 drafter in fp16 (exact
 residual-stream rescale)

The bf16-trained DFlash2 drafter (incoai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2, mirrored as
z-lab/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2) overflows fp16: its residual stream passes 65504
within two layers, turns into inf/NaN, every candidate id becomes 0..top_k-1
and acceptance is exactly zero (vllm-project/vllm#55250). gfx906 has no bf16,
so every DFlash2 run on this fork was in fp16 -- the cause of the "dead for
this family" verdict in docs/gfx906/DEVLOG-dflash2.md.

Every branch reads the residual stream through an RMSNorm, the final norm
feeds the candidates and the selector, and the grouped conv's finish is
linear in the branch output, so scaling o_proj, the up half of gate_up_proj
and down_proj (and the layer-0 residual) by a power of two shrinks the whole
stream without changing anything the draft computes. Applied at load time
for fp16 drafts only; VLLM_DFLASH2_FP16_RESIDUAL_DIVISOR=1 turns it off.

Tests: exactness in fp32, and an fp16 draft whose stream overflows plain
fp16 stays finite and matches fp32 after the rescale.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Sami <247917809+0c33@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 tests/v1/spec_decode/test_dflash2.py        | 157 ++++++++++++++++++++
 vllm/model_executor/models/qwen3_dflash2.py |  50 +++++++
